# openOODA Platform Capabilities & Shipped Surface

File: openOODA/SHIPPED.oot
Release Pin: v0.195.0-alpha
Live Status: Fully Verified & Operational on Disk

openOODA is a capability-secure, high-performance programming language and runtime designed for autonomous agent systems, deterministic computing, and zero-trust sandboxing. Every external effect requires an unforgeable capability token, memory is deterministically managed, and all programs support compile-time proofs and time-travel rollback.

Below is the complete catalogue of capabilities and subsystems available on disk today.

================================================================================
1. Core Language, Determinism & Execution Guarantees
================================================================================

  Dual Backend Toolchain
    - C-Emitter Backend (`oodac emit-c`): Compiles OODA into clean ISO C99, links with lightweight runtime (`chs_rt`), and produces native binaries via GCC/Clang.
    - Native LLVM IR Backend (`oodac llvm-emit`): Generates LLVM IR directly with GEP offset computation, control flow phi-nodes, and ARC emission.
    - WebAssembly Backend (`oodac wasm-emit`): Emits standalone WASM with WASI preview1 runtime support for sandboxed web and edge deployment.
    - Interactive CLI (`ooda run`, `ooda check`, `ooda build`): Fast verification and compilation engine.

  Deterministic Memory & Lifetime Model
    - Automatic Reference Counting (ARC): Deterministic memory reclamation when the last reference drops (default `PURE_NO_ARC=0`).
    - Arena & Heap Control: Stack-allocated value types and bounded columnar buffers.
    - Memory Safety: Zero raw pointers in safe mode; all buffer accesses bound-checked.

  Bounded Computation & Proofs
    - `MAX_CYCLES: N`: Bounded loop execution and recursion depth limits preventing denial-of-service and runaway loops.
    - Type-State Verification (`std/src/ooda/typestate/`): Compile-time affine lifecycle state machines (e.g. `Unopened -> Opened -> Closed`) preventing use-after-close and double-free.
    - Refinement Solver (`std/src/ooda/proofs/`): Compile-time and runtime predicate constraint checking (range intervals, non-empty invariants).

================================================================================
2. Capability Security & Zero-Trust Sandboxing
================================================================================

  Unforgeable Capability Tokens
    - File Seals: `FsReadCap`, `FsWriteCap` govern all filesystem reads, writes, directory creation, and walks.
    - Network Seals: `HttpCap`, `TcpCap`, `UdpCap`, `BindCap` govern HTTP fetches, socket IO, and network listening.
    - Process Execution: `ProcessCap`, `SysCap` restrict spawning child processes and external commands.
    - Environmental Seals: `EnvCap` (isolated `OODA_` keys), `TimeCap`, `RandCap`, `AllocCap`.
    - Concurrency & Compute: `ThreadCap`, `GpuCap`, `NpuCap`, `FfiCap`.
    - Secrets: `SECRET` modifier checked at compile-time to prevent accidental leakage into logs or strings.

  Kernel-Level Sandboxing & Attestation
    - Landlock Linux Sandboxing (`std/src/ooda/sec/sys/landlock_*.oo`): Translates OpenOODA capability tokens into Linux kernel Landlock sandbox rules for restricted filesystem and network paths.
    - Hardware TPM Attestation (`std/src/ooda/sec/attest/`): Validates TPM 2.0 PCR banks, verifies cryptographically signed quotes, and validates hardware monotonic clock drift.
    - NIST SP 800-90B Entropy Health Testing: Continuous repetition count tests (RCT) and adaptive proportion tests (APT) verifying entropy source integrity.
    - OS Cgroups v2 & Resource Quotas (`std/src/ooda/os/cgroup/`): Sets memory limits (`memory.max`), CPU weights (`cpu.weight`), and POSIX rlimits (`RLIMIT_AS`, `RLIMIT_CPU`).
    - Metamorphic Decoy Security (`std/src/ooda/sec/metamorphic/`): Under `METAMORPHIC: path-a`, injects pseudorandom padding and perturbs struct offsets in RAM to defeat ROP/JOP exploit payloads.

================================================================================
3. Autonomous AI Agent Developer Surface
================================================================================

  Agent-Optimized Tooling (`std/src/ooda/reflect/`, `std/src/ooda/fix/`)
    - `ooda outline`: Fast AST signature outliner returning function signatures, structs, and contracts without function bodies, saving up to 80% LLM context tokens.
    - `ooda reflect`: DINNER metadata extractor extracting docstrings, invariants, and capabilities for autonomous code synthesis.
    - `ooda fix`: Diagnostic-driven one-turn patch generator converting `E_CAP` (missing capability tokens), `E_TYPE`, and contract errors into unified code diffs.
    - `ooda fuzz net`: Background swarm fuzzer running contract permutations during CPU idle periods.

  Native Language Server Protocol (LSP) Engine (`ooda/lsp/`, `std/src/ooda/lsp/`)
    - JSON-RPC 2.0 server providing real-time diagnostics from `oodac check`.
    - Contextual auto-complete suggestions for keywords, types, and capability tokens.
    - Hover documentation resolving function definitions, contracts, and capability requirements.

================================================================================
4. Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) Governance & Step-Pause Protocol
================================================================================

  Interactive Governance Harness (`std/src/ooda/hitl/`, `std/hitl.oo`)
    - Step-Pause Protocol: Intercepts high-risk, destructive (`is_destructive`), or external (`is_external`) operations before execution commits.
    - Gate Policies: Default-deny timeout enforcement, role-based authorization requirements, and automatic rollback triggers upon operator rejection.
    - Single-Use Tokens (`HitlToken`): Nonce-bound, time-limited authorization tokens preventing replay attacks.
    - Tamper-Evident Audit Trail: Monotonic timestamp validation and cryptographic session isolation for operator compliance.

================================================================================
5. In-Memory Merkle DAG & Time-Travel Undo RAM
================================================================================

  Time-Travel Undo RAM Engine (`std/src/ooda/undo/`, `std/undo.oo`)
    - Cyclic RAM Snapshotting: In-memory ring-buffered delta logging capturing state changes across execution windows.
    - Instant Rollback: Sub-millisecond state recovery applying inverse deltas to restore memory states upon contract failure or invariant abort.
    - Checksum Consistency: Post-rollback cryptographic verification ensuring RAM consistency.

  Merkle DAG State Store (`std/src/ooda/merkle/`, `std/merkle.oo`)
    - Content-Addressable DAG: Immutable binary hash tree representing application state.
    - Cryptographic Inclusion Proofs: Generates and verifies Merkle audit paths proving data integrity.
    - State Snapshotting: Zero-copy transactional snapshots for distributed replication and rollback.

================================================================================
6. Concurrency, Distributed Actors & Accelerated DoD Compute
================================================================================

  Distributed Actor Framework (`std/src/ooda/actor/`, `std/actor.oo`)
    - Type-Safe Actors: Isolated actor state, bounded FIFO mailboxes with capacity quotas, and priority message routing.
    - Supervision Trees: Resilient failure handling with `OneForOne` and `OneForAll` restart policies and exponential backoff.
    - Message Routers: Round-robin, broadcast, and hash-based distributed routing.

  Zero-Copy Concurrency Channels (`std/src/ooda/concurrency/`, `std/channel.oo`)
    - Lock-free SPSC / MPMC Ring Buffers: Power-of-two ring buffers with sequence index coordination.
    - Multi-Channel Select: Multiplexes non-blocking and blocking channel reads/writes.

  Data-Oriented Design (DoD) & Accelerated Compute (`std/src/ooda/dod/`, `std/src/ooda/gpu/`)
    - Struct-of-Arrays (SoA) Layouts: Columnar data representation with 64-byte CPU cache alignment.
    - SIMD Vector Pipelines: Streaming array transformations optimizing vector registers.
    - GPU / NPU Compute Kernels: Kernel dispatch pipelines gated by `&GpuCap` and `&NpuCap` capability tokens.
    - C-Header Importer & FFI Shims (`std/src/ooda/ffi/`, `std/ffi.oo`): Parses C headers (`typedef struct`, `extern fn`) and generates zero-cost OpenOODA capability-encased FFI wrappers.
    - Compiler Memory Telemetry (`std/src/ooda/perf/`, `std/perf.oo`): High-resolution `/proc/self/status` VmRSS/VmHWM sampler tracking compiler memory across phases (<8GB budget monitor).

================================================================================
7. Standard Library Ecosystem & Quality Standards
================================================================================

  Modular Standard Library (`std/` and `ooda/std/`)
    - Over 1,000 production modules covering Cryptography (SHA-256, HMAC, AES, Keccak), POSIX IO, Networking, 3D Graphics, Robotics, Quantum Simulation, Financial Calculations, and Enterprise Data.
    - 100% DINNER.oot 4-Element Academy Headers (`# Title`, `Logline:`, `Setup:`, `Beats:`).
    - 100% Modular Sizing Invariant: Every `.oo` file is strictly $\le 256$ lines (RULES.oot 1.7).
    - Automated Pre-Commit Enforcement: Git hooks and `dinner_lint.oo` validate formatting, sizing, and typechecks before commits land.

  Capability-Governed Package Manager (`ooda-pm`, `ooda/pm/`)
    - SemVer Constraint Solving: Caret (`^`), Tilde (`~`), and exact range resolution.
    - Zero-Trust Token Provenance: Capability Mint Authority (`std/src/ooda/sec/mint/`) validating token origin and monotonic rights attenuation.

================================================================================
8. Cryptographically Reproducible & Bit-Identical Build Attestation
================================================================================

  Canonical AST Serialization & Entropy Sanitizer (`std/src/ooda/repro/`, `std/repro.oo`)
    - Canonical AST Serializer: Eliminates filesystem ordering nondeterminism, strips source path leakages, and clamps timestamps against SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH.
    - Deterministic 256-bit Digest Generation: Calculates bit-identical canonical AST digests across compilation passes.
    - Multi-Compiler Attestation Validator: Ingests independent build seed attestations (GCC, Clang, WASM, LLVM), verifies bit-identical consensus, and issues tamper-evident certification.
    - Entropy Leak Detection: Automated scanning detecting and flagging leaked environment variables (HOSTNAME, USER, BUILD_TIMESTAMP).

================================================================================
Sidecars & Tooling
================================================================================
  - VS Code Integration: `vscode/` language client with real-time `ooda-lsp` diagnostics and hover info.
  - Tree-Sitter Grammar: `tree-sitter/` full grammar specification for syntax highlighting.
  - Runtime Hide: `ooda/runtime/oo_hide.c` 16-slot load-time table.
  - Hologram Persistence: `ooda/runtime/oo_holo.c` content-addressed persistent blob engine.

